Node js is a v8 engine if javascript.

What is Node.js?
  *Node.js is a JavaScript runtime environment built on Chrome's V8 engine.
  *It lets JavaScript run outside the browser (mainly server-side).
  *Created by Ryan Dahl in 2009.
  *Node.js = V8 engine + extra APIs (file system, networking, etc.)
   Key Characteristics

1. Single-threaded
   > Runs on a single main thread.
   > Handles concurrency via the event loop and async callbacks.

2. Non-blocking I/O (Asynchronous)
  >File read, DB query, network calls — all I/O operations are non-blocking.
  >One request doesn't wait for another to finish — improves performance.
  >Main reason Node.js is fast for I/O-heavy applications.

3. Event-Driven Architecture
   >Works on events + callbacks.
   >Uses the EventEmitter pattern internally.

4. Event Loop (important topic)
   >Call Stack → Node APIs → Callback Queue → Event Loop → back to Call Stack
   >Manages all asynchronous operations.
   >Phases: Timers → Pending Callbacks → Poll → Check → Close Callbacks.

5. NPM (Node Package Manager)
  * Comes bundled with Node.js.
  * World's largest software package registry.
  * Install packages with: npm install <package-name>
  * Core Built-in Modules
          Module	                   Use
           http	               Create web servers
            fs	               File system operations
           path	                Handle file paths
          events	              Event emitter
           os	                  OS-level information
           crypto              	Hashing / encryption

Simple Example — HTTP Server

 const http = require('http');

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(200, {'Content-Type': 'text/plain'});
  res.end('Hello from Node.js!');
});

server.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

Why Node.js Matters for Blockchain Dev
Hardhat, Truffle, Ethers.js, Web3.js — all run on Node.js.
Smart contract deployment scripts are written in JS/Node.
Backend for dApps (APIs connecting to blockchain) commonly uses Node.js + Express.
